          "claim": "Nearly all of ts-food-service's outgoing client calls failed in the incident (about 860 errors) at about 15-19ms each."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT count(*) AS n, sum(CASE WHEN c.attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS parent_errors FROM (SELECT * FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-train-food-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server') s JOIN (SELECT span_id, attr_status_code FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-food-service' AND attr_span_kind='Client') c ON s.parent_span_id=c.span_id",
          "claim": "Train-food server spans all return 200 and link to food client spans, 1719 of which are errors, so the failure is on the food side of the exchange."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-food-service' AND level='SEVERE' AND message LIKE '%Unexpected end of file from server%'",
          "claim": "ts-food-service logged about 860 SEVERE errors reading 'Unexpected end of file from server' from ts-train-food-service."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_source, attr_destination, round(sum(value),1) AS total FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric='hubble_drop_total' AND attr_source LIKE '%food%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Hubble drop counters for the food-service pod show only 48 total, with no drops on the food-to-train-food connection, so this is not packet loss."
